<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P08236">
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta-glucuronidase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P08236" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_GUSB_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">BGLR_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta-G1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GUSB</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3.2.1.31</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P08236_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_dip_DIP-29724N_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot/E9PCV0</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">BGLR_HUMAN Reviewed; 651 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Plays an important role in the degradation of dermatanand keratan sulfates.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=a beta-D-glucuronoside + H2O = an alcohol + D-glucuronate; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:17633, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377,ChEBI:CHEBI:30879, ChEBI:CHEBI:58720, ChEBI:CHEBI:83411;EC=3.2.1.31;ACTIVITY REGULATION: Inhibited by L-aspartic acid.SUBUNIT: Homotetramer.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Lysosome.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;Name=1; Synonyms=Long;IsoId=P08236-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2; Synonyms=Short;IsoId=P08236-2; Sequence=VSP_001799;Name=3;IsoId=P08236-3; Sequence=VSP_054830;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;PTM: N-linked glycosylated with 3 to 4 oligosaccharide chains.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:12754519, ECO:0000269|PubMed:16335952,ECO:0000269|PubMed:19159218}.DISEASE: Mucopolysaccharidosis 7 (MPS7) [MIM:253220]: An autosomalrecessive lysosomal storage disease characterized by inability todegrade glucuronic acid-containing glycosaminoglycans. Thephenotype is highly variable, ranging from severe lethal hydropsfetalis to mild forms with survival into adulthood. Most patientswith the intermediate phenotype show hepatomegaly, skeletalanomalies, coarse facies, and variable degrees of mentalimpairment. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12522561,ECO:0000269|PubMed:12859417, ECO:0000269|PubMed:1702266,ECO:0000269|PubMed:7573038, ECO:0000269|PubMed:7633414,ECO:0000269|PubMed:7680524, ECO:0000269|PubMed:8089138,ECO:0000269|PubMed:8111412, ECO:0000269|PubMed:8111413,ECO:0000269|PubMed:8644704, ECO:0000269|PubMed:8707294,ECO:0000269|PubMed:9099834, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9490302}. Note=Thedisease is caused by mutations affecting the gene represented inthis entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the glycosyl hydrolase 2 family.{ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot.isoform/P08236-2</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_000172</bp:comment>
